<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Département des Forêts</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1795–1814</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">Département</a> des Forêts was a department of the French Republic and Empire from 1795 to 1814, formed from most of the former Duchy of Luxembourg after its annexation by revolutionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Its capital was the city of Luxembourg, and it was named after the forests of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardennes">Ardennes</a>. After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s fall the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> turned most of its territory into the Grand Duchy of Luxembourg, joined in personal union with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/departement-des-forets.jpg" alt="Département des Forêts" width="320" height="249" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Excommunicato (original version by Naturals) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:For%C3%AAts_departement_(1812).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
